{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538017-the-madness-of-mages","id":1538017,"title":"The Madness of Mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-02T20:25:48-07:00","id":1538017,"title":"The Madness of Mages","content":"In M:tA, mages generally go mad (Quiet), when they've built up too much paradox. Now, can a mage be mad, from non-paradox related activities? Apart from buying flaws at character-creation? I know vampires get humanity and derangement-rolls. I guess the nature of the games are different with madness. Are there any mechanics for a mage, to go mad?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T21:04:19-07:00","id":1538024,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s an important metaphysical difference between quiet and real mental illnesses. I\u2019ll leave discussion of actual mental illnesses to those who have a better understanding of them. <br /> <br /> For Quiet, though, there is no break between the mage\u2019s mind and the world around him because he\u2019s actually altering the world around him. He hasn\u2019t lost control of his mind or his senses, he\u2019s let his magic get out of control.<br /> <br /> The Terry Pratchett book Masquerade has a good potential example of this. Without spoiling the actual story, witches have the ability to ignore things like swords. They can shield themselves from that but it is dangerous. They run the risk of forgetting that swords are supposed to hurt, and if they go down that path they\u2019ll eventually forget that actions have consequences. Their own power makes them lose touch with reality because they don\u2019t have to live there. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-03T00:27:33-07:00","id":1538029,"title":"","content":"When a mage goes mad, quiet is essentially how that manifests. There are derangements in Mage as well, and when a mage encounters that \u2018things that man was not meant to know\u2019, suffers a great loss while at 0 or 1 temp willpower, or has their mind barraged either by potent mind magic or other such forces, then there is a risk of madness. They develop a derangement, and with that also may begin a quiet. Even if the quiet ends though, the derangement remains until it is properly addressed, but quiet is now something which could easily return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-03T01:18:17-07:00","id":1538030,"title":"","content":"An illusionist is lost in the desert. Desperate, he creates himself some camel tracks to follow, because one direction is as good as any. Camels know where water is, so he crafts an oasis and fools his senses into quenching his thirst. What now? How about a passing caravan? Some company to ward off going mad is good, even if they are not real.<br /> The caravan takes him to a city where he meets the emir, who is impressed by his adventures and takes him in as a wazir. He enjoys a comfortable life in a privileged position, with luxury and...<br /> .. hold up, what if he's still lying in the dunes, stretching out his dying moments in an elaborate dream he crafted for himself? Does it even matter? Is this new life not vastly preferable, real or not?<br /> <br /> That's Quiet, at least how I see it: the inability to tell where your magic begins and reality ends.<br /> <br /> In contrast, mental illness has different causes. Even for a similar outward result to my example - say, delusion - the cause for Quiet is breaking reality until you are unable to tell there was a difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-03T04:54:42-07:00","id":1538033,"title":"","content":"Also, bear in mind that there's more to Quiet than just Madness. Technocrats, for instance, are more likely to succumb to Denial than to Madness. <br /> <br /> And just as a side note, this topic highlights why I wish we had gotten a <b>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bBook of the Quiet</b> in the same style as <b>Book of the Fallen</b> before Paradox pulled the plug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T17:44:41-07:00","id":1538332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538017-the-madness-of-mages?p=1538030#post1538030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An illusionist is lost in the desert. Desperate, he creates himself some camel tracks to follow, because one direction is as good as any. Camels know where water is, so he crafts an oasis and fools his senses into quenching his thirst. What now? How about a passing caravan? Some company to ward off going mad is good, even if they are not real.<br /> The caravan takes him to a city where he meets the emir, who is impressed by his adventures and takes him in as a wazir. He enjoys a comfortable life in a privileged position, with luxury and...<br /> .. hold up, what if he's still lying in the dunes, stretching out his dying moments in an elaborate dream he crafted for himself? Does it even matter? Is this new life not vastly preferable, real or not?<br /> <br /> That's Quiet, at least how I see it: the inability to tell where your magic begins and reality ends.<br /> <br /> In contrast, mental illness has different causes. Even for a similar outward result to my example - say, delusion - the cause for Quiet is breaking reality until you are unable to tell there was a difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between a mere delusion and Quiet, is that the illusionist will soon be dead while he's imagining that his having a feast with the Sultan.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, not only does the water he drank from his illusionary oasis truly quenches his thirsty, but now his illusionary armies that he commands on behalf of the Sultan are REALLY invading a neighbor country...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 07-09-2024, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T18:09:09-07:00","id":1538334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538017-the-madness-of-mages?p=1538030#post1538030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An illusionist is lost in the desert. Desperate, he creates himself some camel tracks to follow, because one direction is as good as any. Camels know where water is, so he crafts an oasis and fools his senses into quenching his thirst. What now? How about a passing caravan? Some company to ward off going mad is good, even if they are not real.<br /> The caravan takes him to a city where he meets the emir, who is impressed by his adventures and takes him in as a wazir. He enjoys a comfortable life in a privileged position, with luxury and...<br /> .. hold up, what if he's still lying in the dunes, stretching out his dying moments in an elaborate dream he crafted for himself? Does it even matter? Is this new life not vastly preferable, real or not?<br /> <br /> That's Quiet, at least how I see it: the inability to tell where your magic begins and reality ends.<br /> <br /> In contrast, mental illness has different causes. Even for a similar outward result to my example - say, delusion - the cause for Quiet is breaking reality until you are unable to tell there was a difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was beautiful and accurate. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T09:24:31-07:00","id":1538367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538017-the-madness-of-mages?p=1538334#post1538334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was beautiful and accurate. Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish I could claim the story, but I think it's from one of the Earthdawn novels. The magic system in Earthdawn is pretty well done imo, and shares the Pattern approach with Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538017-the-madness-of-mages?p=1538332#post1538332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference between a mere delusion and Quiet, is that the illusionist will soon be dead while he's imagining that his having a feast with the Sultan.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, not only does the water he drank from his illusionary oasis truly quenches his thirsty, but now his illusionary armies that he commands on behalf of the Sultan are REALLY invading a neighbor country...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and that's how you get the really troublesome Marauders. The story doesn't specify at which point illusion and reality start to overlap, but he subconsciously starts to lock out probing that question too deeply because the answer might shatter his complete world. Pulling Mages who are deep in Quiet out of it is so difficult because most will actively avoid it.<br /> <br /> Denial is much more intuitive imo, but I wish I had a good example for Jhor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T19:16:46-07:00","id":1538403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538017-the-madness-of-mages?p=1538367#post1538367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wish I could claim the story, but I think it's from one of the Earthdawn novels. The magic system in Earthdawn is pretty well done imo, and shares the Pattern approach with Mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, and that's how you get the really troublesome Marauders. The story doesn't specify at which point illusion and reality start to overlap, but he subconsciously starts to lock out probing that question too deeply because the answer might shatter his complete world. Pulling Mages who are deep in Quiet out of it is so difficult because most will actively avoid it.<br /> <br /> Denial is much more intuitive imo, but I wish I had a good example for Jhor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jhor isn't intuitive because we don't have a psychological architecture for it.<br /> <br /> Maybe it could be presented as the Superego, with someone passing down heavy judgement on others. A Jhor quiet could be presented as reality destroying everything that the Quiet Mage deems as &quot;unfit&quot;. Given how the force of Entropy is connected with the themes of destruction and rebirth, that's were I would try to start. But yes, I have no idea how to represent that exactly. Denial is interesting - Magic? What are you, superstitious? Poof! Gone.<br /> <br /> What about Jhor? &quot;Criminals are a curse that must be expunged.&quot; And then angry shadows or demons jump are criminals close by and tear them apart? I don't know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T10:33:09-07:00","id":1538434,"title":"","content":"Jhor isn't about wanting to destroy/kill as a means to solve things. It is about an obsession with destruction/death itself. That's why it is counterintuitive. From the three types of Quiet, I think it is the more made up, a mystical malady with no meaningful reflection in actual human experience.<br /> <br /> We have people that really like dark and brooding motifs. But that's no Jhor. We have people with self-destructive or suicidal tendencies, but that's no Jhor either. Serial killers are the closer we have of someone in Jhor, but that seems too much of a simplification of both Serial killers and Jhor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T11:07:01-07:00","id":1538437,"title":"","content":"Well, if we go look at it analogous to the other forms of Quiet we get a Mage so obsessed with death and decay, they no longer care or notice that their own Magick is causing it around them.<br /> <br /> Ironically, the best example I was able to come up with is Jessica Fletcher from Murder, She Wrote. Murders just conveniently happen everywhere she goes, so she can put on her detective cap and solve the mystery.<br /> It's obviously just a handwaved plot device in the show and her interest isn't in death itself, so I'm not totally happy with that example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T12:59:29-07:00","id":1538444,"title":"","content":"Some possible source materials for Jhor:<br /> <br /> Disquiet from Promethean: The Created. - Here destruction manifests through the erosion of trust and social norms. A more obsessive form of this would be Joker's motivations in The Dark Knight.<br /> <br /> The Star Trek TNG episode &quot;Remember Me&quot; where people disappear as if they never existed. - Here Jhor would manifest as the impermanence of the world or of people. The Mandela effect could reasonably be a Jhor manifestation.<br /> <br /> The Dark Tower Series by Stephen King - The way the world has moved on and no longer functions the way it should. Everything looks normalish, but time and space aren't working like they should and things just aren't as reliable as they should be.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T20:48:36-07:00","id":1538458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538017-the-madness-of-mages?p=1538434#post1538434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jhor isn't about wanting to destroy/kill as a means to solve things. It is about an obsession with destruction/death itself. That's why it is counterintuitive. From the three types of Quiet, I think it is the more made up, a mystical malady with no meaningful reflection in actual human experience.<br /> <br /> We have people that really like dark and brooding motifs. But that's no Jhor. We have people with self-destructive or suicidal tendencies, but that's no Jhor either. Serial killers are the closer we have of someone in Jhor, but that seems too much of a simplification of both Serial killers and Jhor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but I wanted to make it a little less silly and less &quot;behold the Lich King&quot; and somewhat more metaphysical. Considering that the game introduces the metaphysical ideas of Dynamism, Stasis and Entropy in a carbon copy of the Hindu triad of Vishnu (creation) Bhrama (permanence) and Shiva (destruction), I was thinking we should go in the same vain.<br /> <br /> Shiva the Destroyer, literally the &quot;Destroyer of Worlds&quot; cited by Oppenheimer, is not an evil and feared deity. On contrary, he is the most worshiped God of Hindu.<br /> <br /> Shiva destroy entire universes - but always with a cosmic purpose. Because he destroys the old so that the new can come to be.<br /> <br /> So, Shiva is not merely a destroyer - he is also the God of rebirth.<br /> <br /> I was thinking something in the same vein, since that's also the view held towards Entropy in Mage.<br /> <br /> Something just crossed my mind now: the idea of <b>Sins Eaters</b>.<br /> <br /> Sins Eaters are beings that consume the &quot;sins&quot; (or &quot;evil&quot; if you will) from others, cleaning others while damning themselves.<br /> <br /> So, Jhor could be something in this vein: Mages obsessed with &quot;cleaning the world&quot;, as opposed to simply edgelord Necromancer liches.<br /> <br /> If you want an example of a character that could be considered as a &quot;Sin Eater&quot;, there's the Ghost Rider from Marvel comics, and also the soldier from hell Spawn. Both are damned to Hell without any possible redemption (well, sort of - you all know how comics work), but regardless of that they still use their demonic powers in order to try to &quot;cleanse the world&quot;. Imho that's more or less what Jhor should do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T06:48:36-07:00","id":1538474,"title":"","content":"One of the things that hit me while I was listing those examples is that while many Quiets push a new reality that the mage thinks should be true, there is room for Quiets that push a reality that the mage doesn't want to be true. These would be Quiets that create a reality for the mage to fight against. Instead of creating a wrongness that the mage can't see, they create a wrongness that he sees all too clearly.<br /> <br /> This could be an element of any of the three types of Quiet, but it is quite well suited for Jhor where the obsession with death and destruction could manifest as either the wrongness that needs to be fought or the solution to the wrongness that needs to be fought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T07:44:12-07:00","id":1538478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538017-the-madness-of-mages?p=1538474#post1538474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things that hit me while I was listing those examples is that while many Quiets push a new reality that the mage thinks should be true, there is room for Quiets that push a reality that the mage doesn't want to be true. These would be Quiets that create a reality for the mage to fight against. Instead of creating a wrongness that the mage can't see, they create a wrongness that he sees all too clearly.<br /> <br /> This could be an element of any of the three types of Quiet, but it is quite well suited for Jhor where the obsession with death and destruction could manifest as either the wrongness that needs to be fought or the solution to the wrongness that needs to be fought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting idea. Like, a healer who subconsciously creates diseases to battle, or someone in Denial who creates anomalies they can research and explain 'rationally'?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think about how Paradox would work for a Marauder of that type, because they would create contradicting effects in their reality zone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538017-the-madness-of-mages?p=1538458#post1538458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Jhor could be something in this vein: Mages obsessed with &quot;cleaning the world&quot;, as opposed to simply edgelord Necromancer liches.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting how Jhor concepts seem to veer towards nihilistic or existentialist approaches, something I would usually reserve for Nephandi. For who btw, I never considered how Quiet works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T06:51:11-07:00","id":1538514,"title":"","content":"It's Morbidity, not Jhor. Jhor is a type of Resonance, of the Elemental flavor. <br /> <br /> In my own games, I've retained the notion that Quiet doesn't always manifest as madness (lower-case \u201cm\u201d); but I've removed the Madness/Denial/Morbidity triad as a holdover from MRev. Instead, Quiet is influenced by your Resonance. If you want to subdivide Quiet into types, they generally follow the flavors of Resonance: a Temperamental Resonance leads to a Quiet akin to what's called Madness, with the specific nature of the Quiet being reflective of exactly what the Temperamental Resonance is. A Stabilizing Resonance leads to a Quiet along the lines of Denial, reinforcing whichever aspect of reality the Resonance describes. An Elemental Resonance leads to a Quiet where the particular element in question takes on an exaggerated role in everything; and if that Resonance is Jhor, the result resembles Morbidity.<br /> <br /> And finally, a Devotional Resonance leads to a Quiet where people's behavior is punished or rewarded in accordance with your chosen cause: at the most subtle, bad things happen to people who oppose what you think is right and good things happen to those who support your preferred ethics; at the other extreme, Hobgoblins might manifest as literal avenging angels or demons punishing the wicked. <br /> <br /> The common ground in all of these is that Quiet is fundamentally about how the mage reacts when the world doesn't work the way she thinks it ought to work. <br /> <br /> This same model can exactly reproduce Madness, Denial, and Morbidity by using Synergy instead of Resonance; though I prefer not to go that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}